"""
Voidloader - the local-model chat app with the Studio shell.

Single-file Tkinter app that runs local .gguf models in-process through llama-cpp-python (CUDA
build) and / or its own built-in loader (Settings > Backends). The window is a rail of workspaces (Chat, Draw, Music, Images, Projects, Blocks,
Power, Settings), an inspector on the right with the controls for whichever workspace is open,
a VRAM bar across the top (click it for the Memory panel), a dock at the bottom (Memory, Load output,
Console) and a command palette
(Ctrl+K). Everything underneath is the same code as before: the local llama.cpp backend, the HTTP
API and phone app, the Block Editor, the Drawing / Music / Images / Power tools and the console.

Needs: Python 3.9+, tkinter, and llama-cpp-python OR the built-in loader (numpy, regex, jinja2; CuPy for the GPU).
Optional: flask (Block Editor), numpy,
pillow, sd-cli.exe + checkpoint (Images), Windows PowerShell (Power Monitor).

Keep GGUFllama_Phone.html next to this file for the phone app.

Run:  python GGUFllama_Studio.py   (first asks how many GB of VRAM you have, then Y/N)
      Keys: Ctrl+K palette, ` (backtick) console, Esc stops a job
"""

